WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.384 --> 00:00:14.326
Grandfather looked from Heidi and Clara to Grandmamma.

2
00:00:15.387 --> 00:00:20.711
They were all sitting at the table outside Grandfather's hut and it was time for Clara to get

3
00:00:20.771 --> 00:00:21.472
ready to go.

4
00:00:21.492 --> 00:00:26.276
"I've been thinking," Grandfather said to Grandmamma.

5
00:00:26.296 --> 00:00:31.120
"If you are willing, Clara can stay here.

6
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.842
We can make a soft bed for her just like Heidi's upstairs."

7
00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:38.463
Grandmamma wasn't sure.

8
00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:42.504
Clara and Heidi watched her eagerly as she thought.

9
00:00:44.345 --> 00:00:49.527
After a pause, she decided it would do no harm for Clara to stay up on the mountain,

10
00:00:50.688 --> 00:00:55.330
and it would be less tiring for her not to be carried up and down from Dorfli every

11
00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.951
day. "Your offer is very kind," she said.

12
00:00:59.971 --> 00:01:01.012
"I agree."

13
00:01:05.068 --> 00:01:06.569
The girls were overjoyed.

14
00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:13.812
Grandfather set to work making Clara's bed, and Grandmamma made sure she had lots of warm blankets for

15
00:01:13.852 --> 00:01:14.252
the night.

16
00:01:15.213 --> 00:01:18.194
They made arrangements for Grandmamma to return in a week.

17
00:01:19.295 --> 00:01:24.797
When the men arrived with Grandmamma's horse, she said goodnight to Grandfather and thanked him again.

18
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:30.760
"I am sure she will grow stronger here," Grandfather said.

19
00:01:31.776 --> 00:01:36.339
Grandfather woke up early the next morning to prepare a picnic for Clara and Heidi.

20
00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.843
He wheeled Clara's chair out in front of the hut and then made them a lunch.

21
00:01:43.724 --> 00:01:50.069
When Peter arrived and saw Clara's wheelchair waiting outside, he knew it meant Clara was coming up the

22
00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:54.912
mountain. He looked around to complain to someone, but no one was around.

23
00:01:56.754 --> 00:02:00.036
In a burst of anger, Peter gave the chair a mighty kick.

24
00:02:01.148 --> 00:02:05.810
It went flying down the mountainside and smashed far below against some rocks.

25
00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:13.393
"Clara will have to go away now," he thought, "and it will be just me and Heidi again."

26
00:02:15.554 --> 00:02:18.975
Inside the hut, Grandfather was feeding the girls breakfast.

27
00:02:20.156 --> 00:02:23.337
Clara finished another big bowlful of the delicious milk.

28
00:02:23.357 --> 00:02:26.399
"It's curious," she said.

29
00:02:26.419 --> 00:02:34.130
"For as long as I can remember, I have eaten only because I had to, but this morning

30
00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.371
I woke up with a real appetite."

31
00:02:38.371 --> 00:02:42.373
When the three came out of the hut, they could not find Clara's wheelchair.

32
00:02:42.393 --> 00:02:45.955
"It must have been the wind," said Heidi.

33
00:02:45.975 --> 00:02:49.016
"Maybe it rolled down the mountain."

34
00:02:49.036 --> 00:02:53.718
"Now, we won't be able to go," said Clara sadly.

35
00:02:54.758 --> 00:02:58.300
But Grandfather wasn't going to let the two little girls down.

36
00:03:00.152 --> 00:03:02.733
"I can carry Clara on my back this time.

37
00:03:03.814 --> 00:03:04.934
But where's Peter?

38
00:03:05.494 --> 00:03:07.375
Daisy and Dusky are still here.

39
00:03:08.436 --> 00:03:10.016
We will have to take them with us."

40
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:16.539
The girls were thrilled with the news, and they all set off up the mountainside with the two

41
00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:17.279
happy goats.

42
00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:26.003
Up on the mountain, Heidi found a sunlit spot, and Grandfather settled Clara comfortably onto the grass.

43
00:03:27.204 --> 00:03:31.399
Then, he headed back down to see what he could discover about Clara's wheelchair.

44
00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:36.082
The sky was deep blue and not a single cloud could be seen.

45
00:03:37.823 --> 00:03:43.307
The snow field higher up on the mountain sparkled as if sprinkled with thousands of silver stars.

46
00:03:44.627 --> 00:03:50.291
After chatting happily with Clara for a few hours, Heidi wanted to wander about to pick flowers.

47
00:03:50.311 --> 00:03:55.995
"Would you think me unkind, Clara, if I left you for a few minutes?"

48
00:03:56.515 --> 00:03:57.076
asked Heidi.

49
00:03:58.168 --> 00:04:03.612
Clara kindly agreed, and Heidi ran off in search of the brightly colored blossoms she loved.

50
00:04:05.473 --> 00:04:10.497
As Clara rested by herself, she found an unexpected pleasure in sitting all alone.

51
00:04:11.778 --> 00:04:16.081
She picked some fresh grass and waved it at Daisy who was grazing nearby.

52
00:04:16.101 --> 00:04:19.984
"Here Daisy, here Daisy," she called.

53
00:04:21.745 --> 00:04:25.448
The goat wandered over and Clara wiggled the grass under the goat's nose.

54
00:04:26.508 --> 00:04:28.952
Daisy snorted happily and Clara laughed.

55
00:04:30.014 --> 00:04:35.021
For the first time, she felt a great desire to be independent and to be able to help

56
00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:38.727
others instead of everyone having to look after her.
